# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: "statement-store: reject submissions from accounts with a depleted allowance"

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      `Store::submit` accepted any allowance present in chain state, including one depleted on
      the count or size axis. A depleted allowance stores nothing by definition, but the
      per-account constraint check only evaluates `max_count` while walking the account's
      existing statements, so an account with a `max_count` of zero and no statements yet had
      nothing to walk and its first statement was admitted. The statement was evicted again by
      the next allowance enforcement pass, so the effect was a single statement stored for an
      account entitled to none.

      Submissions from an account whose allowance is depleted are now rejected up front with
      `RejectionReason::NoAllowance`, the same result already returned for an account with no
      allowance at all.

crates:
  - name: sc-statement-store
    bump: patch
